body:
The fabric gPTP plane measures the propagation delay once a second at nanosecond resolution. The datapath publishes that value to the protocol processor's GET_AVB_INFO answer (`hdl/milan/milan_datapath.sv`, the `propagation_delay` / `eff_gptp_pdelay_w` arm). Each nanosecond change therefore triggers an unsolicited GET_AVB_INFO notification to every registered controller. On the bench the value moves between 375 and 387 ns, so one notification goes out almost every second. The notification itself is correctly rate-limited and sent only on change.

Owner decision 2026-10-17: publish the propagation delay with hysteresis, so jitter of a few nanoseconds does not count as a change.

Done when:
- the published propagation delay changes only when the measured value moves past a stated hysteresis from the last published value, with that bound derived and documented from the measured pdelay jitter;
- a real step, such as a link to a different peer, is still published within one measurement;
- a simulation case shows jitter inside the bound causing no notification, and a step outside it causing exactly one;
- the bench count of unsolicited GET_AVB_INFO notifications over 60 s with a steady link is recorded before and after the change.
